summary: Answered the founder's "you have to be able to SEE THE WEAVE" gap. Designed the two missing navigation surfaces in docs/private/paradigm.pen — the FABRIC (woven commit-history with the oracle verdict on each weave node) and the LIFELINE (one symbol's continuous thread = blame-by-meaning, with the git-blame ghost shattering at the rename/move) — then converged the team's product POV + the founder's view into docs/warpline/pov.html. All grounded in this repo's real topology + real .loom/oracle.jsonl verdicts; honesty cut-line held throughout (render only real data; label forecasts/proxies; lens is lossy).
