body: |-
  DELIVERABLES (task T-2026-06-24-001, Mika-led exploratory design):

  1) FABRIC view — Screen · The Tapestry (paradigm.pen node U5co4, 1400×900). Deterministic railroad woven-history (NO force-directed hairball — would break the determinism thesis). Warp spine (main, amber) + weft feature threads; weave crossings carry the oracle verdict ON the node (calm weft = CONVERGENT, seam KNOT = DIVERGENT); BOLT bands = releases; SELVAGE = HEAD live edge; ∅ rename stitch = lifeline continuity; a dangle severs into the seam void ring. Right inspector decodes the selected DIVERGENT weave: git CLEAN ✓ vs Warpline DIVERGENT, 2×2 confusion matrix with the lit ★ meaning-only cell, THE BREAK (dangle in severed-thread language), and an honest "FIELD OUTCOME — pending (write-path / GAP-7)" block.

  2) LIFELINE view — Screen · The Tapestry — Lifeline (paradigm.pen node QCWef, 1480×740). One symbol's continuous thread through time = blame-by-meaning (warpline lifeline). Real arc: #loom-oracle → renamed #warpline-oracle → package moved packages/loom/ → packages/warpline/. The thread stays UNBROKEN through the ∅ rename + move; a NAME/LOCATION track shows the renames while the thread holds; the git-blame GHOST beneath shatters into 3 spans mis-attributing authorship to the mechanical rename/move commits. Bottom contrast panels: Warpline meaning-attribution (loid, correct) vs git blame (ascend / 'rename Loom→Warpline' commit, wrong).

  3) POV HTML — docs/warpline/pov.html. A strategic point-of-view page (distinct from index.html's vision and system.html's map) converging the 4-lens product panel + the founder's view, on the shared token system/nav/footer/reveal patterns. Sections: Thesis (WARP is truth, bytes a projection — with Arky's lossy-lens honesty caveat) · Where it stands today (built/designed/latent/not-yet, no vaporware) · THE GATE (read-only is the trap; write path + GAP-7 = the gate; companion-first "Warpline Guard" CI check, replacement by gravity) · The Wedge (AI-agent-heavy TS teams; this repo = user zero) · The Moat (non-portable calibration corpus; "the clock hasn't started" — moat starts when the write path ships) · The Surfaces (inline Fabric + Lifeline SVGs answering the founder's question) · The Path (a 5-rung roadmap ladder, each rung gating the next). Validated: 7 sections, 2 SVGs, balanced markup, all CSS tokens resolve.

  HONESTY DISCIPLINE (held throughout): the divergent hero in the Fabric is a labeled `weave --preview` forecast (real engine output), NOT a faked landed merge — the repo's real merges (loom-engine→main) are genuinely CONVERGENT in oracle.jsonl. Trust/field-outcome/WeaveRecord shown only as "pending (write-path)", never fabricated. Tapestry/Bridge/Lightbox remain write-path + Classroom-gated per the design-system spec.

  CAVEATS / FOLLOW-ONS: Lifeline's symbol-picker is a designed stub (interaction not specified); Fabric lane topology is slightly simplified for the mockup (trunk drawn full-height); these are DESIGN artifacts — wiring the Fabric/Lifeline into the live Platform warpline section (binding GET /refs + git topology + oracle.jsonl) is a separate BUILD task, and the honest read-only-now scope is: real git branch/merge/tag topology + per-merge oracle verdicts.
